pnpm-debug.log*
logs/
*.log

# Environment — never commit secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Tally — personal financial data must NEVER be committed.
# Encrypted backups, exported ledgers and any real bank statements stay local.
*.tally
*.csv
# The `.example.csv` suffix marks a hand-written synthetic fixture — invented
# merchants, invented amounts, no real statement ever. Those are the only CSVs
# that may be committed, and they must be, because the import tests are worth
# nothing without them.
#
# This escape hatch was previously written as `!docs/samples/*.example.csv`,
# which covered the web app's copies and silently excluded the Android test
# resources. The result was five import tests that passed locally and failed on
# CI with "test resource not found" — the fixtures existed on one disk and in no
# commit. Matching on the suffix anywhere keeps the strict rule (a real
# statement is never named `.example.csv`) without depending on a directory
# list that the next copy will fall outside of again.
!**/*.example.csv

# QA verification artefacts (screenshots from emulated-device runs)
qa-screenshots/

# Android — local build output and machine-specific SDK path.
# gradlew / gradlew.bat / gradle/wrapper/* ARE committed on purpose so CI
# needs no bootstrap step.
android/.gradle/
android/**/build/
android/local.properties
android/.idea/
android/*.iml
android/**/.cxx/
android/captures/

